## Story Description
backend/tests/test_cube_api.py has 9 failing tests. All fail because VALID_TOKEN = 'valid.jwt.token' is not a real JWT so middleware's pyjwt.get_unverified_header() raises an exception, token_alg becomes 'unreadable', the JWKS path is taken, SUPABASE_URL is not set, and a 401 is returned before any test logic runs. The patch target 'app.middleware.auth.jwt.decode' is also wrong — the middleware imports 'import jwt as pyjwt' so the name to patch is 'app.middleware.auth.pyjwt.decode'. Additionally, _make_supplier_rows() builds dicts without 'abc_segment', but the endpoint now accesses r['abc_segment'] (added in DATA_ACCURACY_FIXES sprint), which would KeyError after the JWT fix is applied. The reference fix pattern is in backend/tests/test_ingestion_api.py.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_cube_api.py — add 'import jwt as _jwt' to the imports section (after 'import uuid')
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_cube_api.py — add '_JWT_SECRET = "test-secret"' constant after the imports block
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_cube_api.py — change 'VALID_TOKEN = "valid.jwt.token"' to 'VALID_TOKEN = _jwt.encode({"email": TEST_EMAIL}, _JWT_SECRET, algorithm="HS256")'
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_cube_api.py — change every occurrence of 'monkeypatch.setenv("SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET", "secret")' to 'monkeypatch.setenv("SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET", _JWT_SECRET)' (there are 9 such lines, one per test method)
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_cube_api.py — change every occurrence of 'patch("app.middleware.auth.jwt.decode"' to 'patch("app.middleware.auth.pyjwt.decode"' (there are 9 such lines)
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_cube_api.py — in _make_supplier_rows(), add '"abc_segment": None' to each dict in the list comprehension, after 'avg_payment_days'
- Run: cd backend && python -m pytest tests/test_cube_api.py -v — all 9 tests must pass

