## Story Description
backend/tests/test_engagements.py has 3 failing tests in TestEngagementsCRUD. The same root cause applies: VALID_TOKEN is not a real JWT and the patch target is wrong. Additionally, _make_client() (a helper defined but not used by the failing tests) patches 'app.middleware.auth.jwt.decode' with a side_effect that imports jose.JWTError — jose is not installed in this project and the function references VALID_TOKEN which must also be updated. The TestAuth class (2 tests) already passes because those tests don't send an Authorization header or don't need the mock to succeed. Only TestEngagementsCRUD tests are failing.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_engagements.py — add 'import jwt as _jwt' to the imports section
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_engagements.py — add '_JWT_SECRET = "test-secret"' constant after the imports block
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_engagements.py — change 'VALID_TOKEN = "valid.jwt.token"' to 'VALID_TOKEN = _jwt.encode({"email": TEST_EMAIL}, _JWT_SECRET, algorithm="HS256")'
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_engagements.py — fix the _make_client() helper: change 'patch("app.middleware.auth.jwt.decode", side_effect=fake_decode)' to 'patch("app.middleware.auth.pyjwt.decode", return_value={"email": TEST_EMAIL})' and remove the fake_decode inner function and the 'from jose import JWTError' line (simplify to a direct return_value patch matching the pattern in test_ingestion_api.py)
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_engagements.py — change every occurrence of 'monkeypatch.setenv("SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET", "secret")' to 'monkeypatch.setenv("SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET", _JWT_SECRET)'
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_engagements.py — change every occurrence of 'patch("app.middleware.auth.jwt.decode"' to 'patch("app.middleware.auth.pyjwt.decode"'
- Run: cd backend && python -m pytest tests/test_engagements.py -v — all 5 tests must pass (2 TestAuth + 3 TestEngagementsCRUD)

